#: Graphs.md:1
msgid "Representing PLUMED inputs using flowcharts"
msgstr "Flow Chart による入力の表示"

#: Graphs.md:3
msgid ""
"Ever since we wrote the PLUMED paper in 2014, I have wondered if we can "
"automate the process of generating diagrams similar to the ones in that "
"paper that show how Values and forces are passed between the various actions"
" in the PLUMED input. If we could automate the generation of these diagrams,"
" we could have similar charts for all the entries in the PLUMED nest. We "
"could also have these diagrams for the example inputs in the tutorials and "
"manuals."
msgstr ""
"2014年の論文以来、Value と力が Action 間を流れる図の自動生成を考えていました。可能なら NEST の全入力や "
"Tutorial・マニュアル例にも付けられます。"

#: Graphs.md:8
msgid ""
"The time to implement these diagrams is now when we have changed the code so"
" that actions can also pass vectors, scalars and grids between them, as "
"discussed [here](Passing.md). I have thus written a command line tool that "
"allows one to generate a graph from a plumed input. Consequentially, if I "
"take the contents of the file plumed.dat below:"
msgstr ""
"[こちら](Passing.md) のように Vector・Scalar・Grid を渡せる改良をした今こそ実装時です。入力から Graph "
"を作るツールを書きました。次の plumed.dat に、"

#: Graphs.md:21
msgid "And run the command:"
msgstr "次を実行すると、"

#: Graphs.md:27
msgid "I can generate the graph shown below:"
msgstr "下の Graph が生成されます。"

#: Graphs.md:39
msgid ""
"The file `graph.md` output by the command above is renderable using "
"[mermaid](https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/flowchart.html). You can see the "
"resulting flow chart if you copy and paste the file's contents "
"[here](https://mermaid.live/). I used Mermaid to build the charts, as you "
"can insert Mermaid syntax into GitHub markdown. The rendered diagrams then "
"appear when GitHub shows the rendered markdown online. The renderer that "
"deals with the PLUMED input files in the manual pages, the PLUMED nest and "
"the PLUMED tutorials site will create the mermaid syntax for you directly "
"from the PLUMED input. You simply need to add the comment `#MERMAID=value` "
"if you want a graph that shows how values are passed through the code like "
"the one above or the comment `#MERMAID=force` if you want a graph that shows"
" how the chain rule is applied to calculate the forces."
msgstr ""
"`graph.md` は [Mermaid](https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/flowchart.html) "
"で表示でき、[こちら](https://mermaid.live/) に貼れます。GitHub Markdown "
"でも描画できるため採用しました。マニュアル・NEST・Tutorial の Renderer は入力から直接生成します。`#MERMAID=value`"
" で値、`#MERMAID=force` で Chain Rule による力の流れを表示します。"

#: Graphs.md:45
msgid ""
"Each node in the diagram above represents one of the actions from the PLUMED"
" input file. The arrows then indicate how PLMD::Value objects are passed "
"between the actions."
msgstr "Node は各 Action、矢印は PLMD::Value の受け渡しです。"

#: Graphs.md:48
msgid "The shape of the node tells you about the type of action:"
msgstr "形は Action の種類を示します。"

#: Graphs.md:50
msgid ""
"Rectangular nodes with only outwards arrows are PUT actions containing data "
"passed from the MD code. These nodes cannot take PLMD::Value objects created"
" in PLUMED as input."
msgstr "外向き矢印だけの矩形は MD データの PUT で、PLUMED 内の Value を入力にできません。"

#: Graphs.md:51
msgid ""
"Rectangular nodes with only inward arrows are actions like PRINT that only "
"take PLMD::Value as arguments. These nodes cannot create PLMD::Value objects"
" and pass them to other actions."
msgstr "内向きだけの矩形は PRINT などで、Value を受けるだけで生成・伝達しません。"

#: Graphs.md:52
msgid ""
"Rounded nodes are actions that can take PLMD::Value objects created within "
"PLUMED as input and pass on such objects as output."
msgstr "角丸は Value を入出力できます。"

#: Graphs.md:54
msgid ""
"The arrows connecting the actions provide information about the PLMD::Value "
"object being passed."
msgstr "矢印は渡される Value の種類を示します。"

#: Graphs.md:56
msgid "Passing of __scalars__ is indicated using __black arrows__"
msgstr "__Scalar__ は __黒__。"

#: Graphs.md:57
msgid "Passing of __vectors__ is indicated using __blue arrows__"
msgstr "__Vector__ は __青__。"

#: Graphs.md:58
msgid "Passing of __matrices__ is indicated using __red arrows__"
msgstr "__Matrix__ は __赤__。"

#: Graphs.md:59
msgid "Passing of __grids__ is indicated using __greeen arrows__"
msgstr "__Grid__ は __緑__。"

#: Graphs.md:60
msgid ""
"Passing of __atomic positions__ is indicated using __violet arrows__. An "
"atomic position is just five PLMD::Value objects that are all vectors. These"
" five vectors contain the x, y and z positions of the atoms and the masses "
"and charges of the atoms."
msgstr "__原子位置__ は __紫__。x・y・z・質量・電荷の5 Vector の PLMD::Value です。"

#: Graphs.md:62
msgid ""
"You can also show how forces are passed between actions by using the "
"command:"
msgstr "力の流れも次で表示できます。"

